      "problem": "Find $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 4}\\log_2 (x+4) .$",
      "worked_solution": "The function $\\log_2 (x+4)$ is defined for $x>-4,$ so the limit as $x \\to 4$ exists.\n\nTo find this limit, we substitute $x=4$ into the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}{log}_{2}⁡(x+4) & ={log}_{2}⁡(4+4) \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(8) \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡({2}^{3}) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
